		<preamble GUID="_7c354baa-44fe-4fef-903f-a4e62a7fe5aa" eId="preamble">
			<?DMS-Component componentId="4605c5b8-6dc5-45bc-b462-54c5cf3b86db" seriesId="7bcd72bb-dff3-442d-85d8-bb756765bafc" versionNumber="1"?>
			<formula GUID="_b11d25a8-4738-4c0b-bb0a-b893157b3e00" eId="preamble__enactingWords" name="enactingText">
				<p>The Secretary of State makes these <ref class="placeholder" href="#varDocSubType"/> in exercise of the powers conferred by section 17A(1), (3), (5) and (6) of the Data Protection Act 2018 (“the 2018 Act”)<authorialNote GUID="_92e75733-d159-4cfb-84be-478686c2389b" class="footnote" eId="fnote_9" marker="9">
					<p>2018 c. 12; section 17A was inserted by S.I. 2019/419, Schedule 2, paragraphs 1 and 23.</p>
					</authorialNote>.</p>
				<p>In accordance with section 17A(1) and (3) of the 2018 Act, the Secretary of State considers that the United States of America ensures an adequate level of protection of personal data for certain transfers.</p>
				<p>In accordance with section 182(2) of the 2018 Act, the Secretary of State has consulted the Commissioner<authorialNote GUID="_6e475754-313f-4858-8852-7cc545b324ea" class="footnote" eId="fnote_10" marker="10">
					<p>“The Commissioner” is defined in section 3(8) of the Data Protection Act 2018.</p>
					</authorialNote> and such other persons as the Secretary of State considers appropriate.</p>
			</formula>
		</preamble>
		<body>
			<?DMS-Component componentId="e6088e21-3b78-4f28-a73b-b6fd5d560723" seriesId="659bd80a-6c78-4888-89de-a8789ca4d257" versionNumber="1"?>
			<hcontainer GUID="_d46cbfbe-3788-438d-8ca4-96f2d3837d46" class="prov1" eId="reg_1" name="regulation">
				<?DMS-Component componentId="9210e689-ba32-4438-a14a-11206b648cd1" seriesId="d4e968ee-f3d0-4f04-b2ca-5807243f7975" versionNumber="1"?>
				<heading GUID="_df901a5d-2f14-4919-b87d-353020003438" eId="reg_1__hdg">Citation, commencement and extent</heading>
				<num>1.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_c6236bc9-9bb7-4bb7-8b6a-82b7554632b4" class="prov2" eId="reg_1__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>These Regulations may be cited as the Data Protection (Adequacy) (United States of America) Regulations 2023.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_0afef83c-9586-486f-b4c0-26ccac5b5a52" class="prov2" eId="reg_1__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<content>
						<p>These Regulations come into force on 12th October 2023.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_e3a6e4f5-2343-4324-aec8-359889f529a1" class="prov2" eId="reg_1__para_3">
					<num>(3)</num>
					<content>
						<p>These Regulations extend to England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_3626c45a-6dc5-40b6-8299-990f67e4bcd8" class="prov1" eId="reg_2" name="regulation">
				<?DMS-Component componentId="a1879e7b-19b4-4919-8eaa-b65277766238" seriesId="371956b3-2dc5-4bd5-85ba-4313a3c0c482" versionNumber="0"?>
				<heading GUID="_3842b003-7939-4d3d-a5f6-6c3d0b6cc54c" eId="reg_2__hdg">Interpretation</heading>
				<num>2.</num>
				<intro GUID="_106460cb-a39b-463c-bb16-1891c8f5e453" eId="reg_2__intro">
					<p>In these Regulations—</p>
				</intro>
				<hcontainer GUID="_76c0dee3-4d76-4a9f-b797-f6171591d1ac" class="definition" eId="reg_2__def_DataPrivacyFrameworkList_" name="definition">
					<content>
						<p><def GUID="_953fb400-4d3f-4911-9527-9f48b2aa7c22" eId="reg_2__def_DataPrivacyFrameworkList" ukl:endQuote="”" ukl:startQuote="“">Data Privacy Framework List</def> means the list of that name, as it has effect from time to time, which is maintained and made publicly available by the United States Department of Commerce<authorialNote GUID="_383acfd0-28dd-43cf-aa18-57dcd0d5b068" class="footnote" eId="fnote_11" marker="11">
							<p>A link to the Data Privacy Framework List can be found at https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/uk-us-data-bridge-data-privacy-framework-principles-and-list. Hard copies can also be inspected during office hours and free of charge at the offices of the Department for Science, Innovation and Technology, 100 Parliament Street, London SW1A 2BQ.</p>
							</authorialNote>;</p>
					</content>
				</hcontainer>
				<hcontainer GUID="_e1339e05-3dfb-4286-a543-3c61b8deccdb" class="definition" eId="reg_2__def_EU-USDataPrivacyFramework_" name="definition">
					<content>
						<p><def GUID="_83369715-71cf-4259-9a25-bbdd3bbc4416" eId="reg_2__def_EU-USDataPrivacyFramework" ukl:endQuote="”" ukl:startQuote="“">EU-US Data Privacy Framework</def> means the programme of that name administered by the United States Department of Commerce;</p>
					</content>
				</hcontainer>
				<hcontainer GUID="_b2332dc1-b9c6-4c62-ae29-c1af2e347d28" class="definition" eId="reg_2__def_EU-USDataPrivacyFrameworkPrinciples_" name="definition">
					<content>
						<p><def GUID="_b610b624-4413-40af-bf51-035aae76999f" eId="reg_2__def_EU-USDataPrivacyFrameworkPrinciples" ukl:endQuote="”" ukl:startQuote="“">EU-US Data Privacy Framework Principles</def> means the principles and supplemental principles issued by the United States Department of Commerce under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework as they apply to transfers of personal data from the United Kingdom under the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework<authorialNote GUID="_bc44783b-c0bf-43a9-ada0-d0f7a61adfa7" class="footnote" eId="fnote_12" marker="12">
							<p>Electronic copies of these principles can be obtained from https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/uk-us-data-bridge-data-privacy-framework-principles-and-list. Hard copies can also be inspected during office hours and free of charge at the offices of the Department for Science, Innovation and Technology, 100 Parliament Street, London SW1A 2BQ.</p>
							</authorialNote>;</p>
					</content>
				</hcontainer>
				<hcontainer GUID="_d4c3929e-d410-4ee9-9593-6e86739f2e54" class="definition" eId="reg_2__def_UKExtensiontotheEU-USDataPrivacyFramework_" name="definition">
					<content>
						<p><def GUID="_0589abbb-83a2-4531-95d2-3ee2a99378ab" eId="reg_2__def_UKExtensiontotheEU-USDataPrivacyFramework" ukl:endQuote="”" ukl:startQuote="“">UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework</def> means the extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework which the United States Department of Commerce administers in relation to transfers of personal data from the United Kingdom.</p>
					</content>
				</hcontainer>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_292e8502-f69c-463a-82b5-6450b0ff026b" class="prov1" eId="reg_3" name="regulation">
				<?DMS-Component componentId="2f45efa6-7c8b-4ad8-8384-bea36a34a426" seriesId="02421d04-6949-4fd2-b830-e048e3d71eec" versionNumber="1"?>
				<heading GUID="_d6d921cd-bf26-44f4-98f3-40ed62a9f5a7" eId="reg_3__hdg">Adequate level of protection</heading>
				<num>3.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_0ce26f40-2efe-4f02-ba22-022fcdb35d7e" class="prov2" eId="reg_3__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>For the purposes of Part 2 of the Data Protection Act 2018<authorialNote GUID="_2a785dff-9e22-4a11-a0f7-c179b911af3e" class="footnote" eId="fnote_3" marker="3">
							<p>2018 c. 12.</p>
							</authorialNote> and the UK GDPR<authorialNote GUID="_63e93c2a-4a43-43db-b1cc-4aa5d3fa4eb9" class="footnote" eId="fnote_4" marker="4">
							<p>The “UK GDPR” is defined in section 3(10) of the 2018 Act.</p>
							</authorialNote>, the Secretary of State specifies the United States of America as ensuring an adequate level of protection of personal data<authorialNote GUID="_06d86ed4-003c-4c89-ba6b-427306db1254" class="footnote" eId="fnote_5" marker="5">
							<p>“Personal data” is defined in Article 4(1) of the UK GDPR and has the same meaning in Part 2 of the 2018 Act by virtue of section 5 of that Act.</p>
							</authorialNote> for a transfer described in paragraph (2).</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_e74f048f-f80d-4621-a61c-3b977b258c24" class="prov2" eId="reg_3__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<intro GUID="_7ebb9ef0-725c-43db-ae1d-461dd6f37e16" eId="reg_3__para_2__intro">
						<p>A transfer described by this paragraph is a transfer of personal data which—</p>
					</intro>
					<level GUID="_679e0fb2-2fb1-4196-ace4-7643bb2fac1c" class="para1" eId="reg_3__para_2__para_a">
						<num>(a)</num>
						<content>
							<p>is to a person in the United States of America who is indicated on the Data Privacy Framework List as participating in the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework; and</p>
						</content>
					</level>
					<level GUID="_31c50b53-f772-44d8-8dd2-7678f0d16489" class="para1" eId="reg_3__para_2__para_b">
						<num>(b)</num>
						<content>
							<p>will be subject to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework Principles on receipt by that person.</p>
						</content>
					</level>
				</paragraph>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_192e90aa-c400-4861-a792-351202133bc8" class="prov1" eId="reg_4" name="regulation">
				<?DMS-Component componentId="c1fe8899-aa9b-40d5-93d3-0d4ccfb70077" seriesId="afd82879-95e5-4ff2-bbb9-d880c6a6168f" versionNumber="1"?>
				<heading GUID="_c2a08614-879f-4294-8438-fec3d7bc3e44" eId="reg_4__hdg">Independent supervisory authorities</heading>
				<num>4.</num>
				<intro GUID="_5b2d190b-ef05-4781-8752-f4862357da1f" eId="reg_4__intro">
					<p>The independent supervisory authorities<authorialNote GUID="_fa81f8d2-e2cd-42ad-aff5-72d49c840355" class="footnote" eId="fnote_6" marker="6">
						<p>Referred to in Article 45(2)(b) of the UK GDPR.</p>
						</authorialNote> for the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework are—</p>
				</intro>
				<level GUID="_9095b888-a1e1-40a8-8981-80c94742e6af" class="para1" eId="reg_4__para_a">
					<num>(a)</num>
					<content>
						<p>the United States Federal Trade Commission; and</p>
					</content>
				</level>
				<level GUID="_ec101f7c-5669-4059-9a9c-7c82387a15ee" class="para1" eId="reg_4__para_b">
					<num>(b)</num>
					<content>
						<p>the United States Department of Transportation.</p>
					</content>
				</level>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_9a9d3618-c10d-4419-a72b-374845d8ac47" eId="sigs" name="signatures">
				<?DMS-Component componentId="d6cf09b9-5136-4aef-a63f-9e2fc73f75af" seriesId="058c3e95-96c7-4bee-8845-3e2b915cc2b9" versionNumber="0"?>
				<hcontainer GUID="_2bac69b5-7d04-4dc6-9088-61492f7648df" eId="sigs__sigBlk" name="signatureBlock">
					<content>
						<block GUID="_80714257-7d1b-463b-bb8d-a7dbf033b3d0" eId="sigs__sigBlk__sig" name="signature">John Whittingdale</block>
						<block GUID="_38870e78-b85d-4cdb-9f20-9f6ec0c00fa5" eId="sigs__sigBlk__role" name="role">Minister of State</block>
						<block name="date"><date date="2023-09-20">20th September 2023</date></block>
